// V changes only its underlying representation (Int -> Long), never its name or kind.
// holder.kt is never edited: it uses V only as a type, so its serialized-IR fingerprint is
// unchanged (V stays a symbolic type reference in the serialized IR, SerializedIrFileFingerprint)
// and its generated code references no symbol of v.kt, so no per-file dependency edge on v.kt
// is recorded. But holder.kt's cached ir/class_fields bakes V's unboxed binary type into
// Holder's object layout and into the calling convention of its constructor and getter.
// When v.kt changes, the dirty-file analysis (fingerprint change + reverse walk over the
// recorded edges) therefore never rebuilds holder.kt. The freshly compiled main then passes a
// Long-backed V (5000000000) into the stale Int-ABI constructor across identical mangled
// names, which truncates it to 705032704 (= 5000000000 mod 2^32) instead of 5000000000.

MODULES: lib, main

STEP 0:
    libs: lib, main
STEP 1:
    libs: lib, main
